   "level": "remember",
   "q": "Define the pinch point in an absorber.",
   "marks": 2,
   "a": "The point where the minimum operating line touches the equilibrium curve; the driving force there is zero."
  },
  {
   "level": "understand",
   "q": "Why does a lower liquid rate need a taller column?",
   "marks": 3,
   "a": "The operating line flattens about the fixed top point, the gap to equilibrium shrinks, and more stages or transfer units are needed; at the minimum the gap closes and the height becomes infinite."
  },
