  {
   "level": "analyze",
   "q": "For a straight equilibrium line through the origin, show the pinch is at the bottom.",
   "marks": 4,
   "a": "Gap = Y_operating − Y* = Y_out + (L/G)(X − X_in) − mX. This falls as X rises because L/G < m, so it is smallest at the largest X, the bottom."
  }
